From cad32e94fd40a59bb1c95c71e5ecb28d897d687b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] policy: provide the compiled fee-hysteresis controller and
 diagnostics

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved source semantics. The candidate repair below
changes this boundary and requires new validation evidence.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Fast-path single-input CheckRegularTransaction duplicate-input checks,
coalesce BlockUndo disk writes, and optimize bulk mempool clear.

Original-Commit: a4ea86865414bbf4f98512bbd4460e2a42897acc
Original-Patch: ecash/020
Split-Concern: fees

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.
Candidate-purpose-redistribution: Place RPC fee-controller diagnostics with the fee-controller implementation; consistency of admission policy requires this owner's gates.

Candidate-Repair: Complete this controller boundary with its matching header from later45 and actual CMake registration. Keep its legacy per-kB policy diagnostics; do not impose an extra fee rejection while the controller is at its base floor, preserving configured upstream admission. Document the historical ConsensusFloor name as relay policy only for eCash. Widen congestion/cushion intermediates and saturate Chronik signed-rate adapters; direct rolling/reset/extreme arithmetic native cases pass13 assertions. Move adaptive connected-block accounting to the later owner that defines RecordConnectedBlock, omitting the already-owned duplicate SMT update. Merge header-only45 here and preserve its provenance; clean build/native/functional/Chronik/runtime gates required.

